#import "/modern-iaf/manuals/layout/manual.typ": *

#idx("Phase 2")#idx("Pattern")Phase 2 of the training course, "Basic handling, the pattern and landing", takes you from your first take-off to the overhead pattern, the go-around and the emergencies of the take-off and the flight. It has eight #term("lesson")s: six day lessons, a night lesson and check ride 2. Each starts cold and dark on the parking spot and ends with the engine shut down on that spot. The briefing and the #term("notebook")'s Lesson tab give each lesson's steps and the figures to hold; the pattern itself is in each jet's flight manual: the #other("f16i", "landing"), the #other("f16d", "landing") and the #other("f35i", "landing").

=== The lessons <pattern-lessons>

#idx("Phase 2, lessons")
#grid-table(
  (auto, 2fr, 1fr),
  ([Lesson], [What it teaches], [Graded]),
  [2.1 Take-off and first flight], [The take-off, the climb, level turns and a straight-in landing.], [the centreline on the take-off roll, the lift-off speed, the gear up after the lift-off, the touchdown point, the sink rate],
  [2.2 The overhead break and landing], [The overhead pattern. In the F-16s the instructor flies the first one ("my controls") and hands the jet back on the runway; in the F-35I the instructor leads it from a second jet ("follow me").], [the pattern's height, the final's angle of attack, the touchdown point, the centreline at touchdown],
  [2.3 Touch-and-go and go-around], [A touch-and-go, closed patterns and a go-around from short final.], [the pattern's height, the final's angle of attack, the lowest height of the go-around],
  [2.4 High AoA and G], [Slow flight, the angle-of-attack and G limiters, and a turn at the corner speed.], [the slow flight's speed, the highest G, the speed in the turn],
  [2.5 Take-off abort and engine fire], [An engine fire on the take-off roll and the abort; after a restart and a second take-off, an engine fire in flight.], [stopped on the runway, the throttle back after the fire light, the emergency steps done],
  [2.6 Flameout and airstart], [A flameout, the air start, and the flameout pattern to a landing.], [the engine started again, the landing on the runway, the emergency steps done],
  [2.7 At night], [The pattern and the landing by night, with the goggles or the helmet's night camera.], [the pattern's height, the final's angle of attack, the touchdown point],
  [2.8 Check ride 2], [Everything of phases 1 and 2, with no calls in flight.], [phases 1 and 2's items],
)

Each item is graded against its standard, with the jet's own figures. The emergencies' steps are on the notebook's EMERGENCY tab.

=== Check ride 2 <pattern-check>

#idx("Check ride")The instructor gives the briefing and the #term("debrief") only: no calls and no switch highlights in flight; the notebook stays with you. One emergency already taught (an engine fire on the roll or in flight, or a flameout) may come at a random time, unannounced. The ride grades the items of phases 1 and 2, but not the night lesson's, since it is flown by day, and an emergency's items only when that emergency came.
